After updating the user profile information in the database, the function logs changes to the audit table to track any changes made to the user's profile. If there is an error logging the changes to the audit table or if the update query fails, the function returns `false` and logs an error message. Otherwise, it returns a success message indicating that the update was successful.

The code uses prepared statements to protect against SQL injection attacks and to optimize performance by reducing the number of database queries required. It also includes rate limiting to prevent abuse and ensure fair usage of system resources.']

