The code also includes error handling for various failure scenarios, such as missing files or invalid transformation rules. It also ensures proper handling of memory allocation and deallocation to avoid leaks. Additionally, it is designed to be modular and easily extended with new types of transformations in the future.

Performance-wise, this code balances efficiency with usability by optimizing performance without compromising readability and maintainability. It also ensures scalability by handling very large configuration files efficiently.']

