The function also includes logging mechanisms to record the creation process and any errors encountered. It is thread-safe and capable of handling concurrent access from multiple threads without data corruption. To achieve this, it uses appropriate synchronization mechanisms such as mutexes or atomic operations.

Furthermore, it integrates the functionality to fetch UE information from an external database (e.g., SQLite) based on RNTI. The database connection is managed efficiently to avoid resource exhaustion, and proper error handling is implemented for database connection failures or timeouts. The function also ensures that the list of elements can handle large volumes of data efficiently by optimizing the database query execution using indexes where appropriate.

The function adheres to best practices for resource management, including proper cleanup of allocated memory and closed database connections. It also logs relevant information for debugging and monitoring purposes.']

