To manage resources efficiently, the function uses efficient allocation and deallocation techniques for downlink data buffers and UE contexts. The `malloc()` and `realloc()` functions are used to allocate and resize memory for these structures, while the `free()` function is used to release unused memory.

The function also supports real-time updates from an external data source using a timer mechanism. The `timer_handler()` function periodically checks for new updates from the external data source and processes them as needed. This allows the system to handle real-time updates within the specified 50 millisecond time frame.

