To handle thread-safety and memory management for the external data source, this code uses a combination of mutex locks and conditional variables to ensure that only one thread can access the external data source at any given time. The `fetchExternalDataFromSource` function is called in a separate thread to fetch external data, while the main thread waits on a condition variable to signal when the external data has been fetched successfully or if an error occurred.

The time complexity of this code is O(n), where n is the number of structures to be created, as each structure is allocated and populated separately using `malloc` and `realloc`. The use of a random number generator ensures that the CRCFLAG is set to 1 for at least 5% of the structures.']

