The octree should support insertion and query operations for efficient spatial data management. Implement a mechanism to balance the octree during insertions to maintain optimal performance. Consider integrating with an external spatial indexing library for additional functionality, such as k-nearest neighbors queries.

Given that this system will be used in a high-traffic simulation environment with real-time requirements, developers must also ensure thread safety when multiple threads are accessing or modifying the octree simultaneously. 

To further complicate matters, your implementation must handle cases where the number of leaf nodes is not a power of two, and the feature size can vary between 16 and 256 bytes. The data capacity can be any positive integer.

**Constraints:**
- The feature size can vary between 16 and 256 bytes.
- The number of leaf nodes can be any positive integer.
- The data capacity can be any positive integer.
- Ensure thread safety when multiple threads are accessing or modifying the octree simultaneously.

**Return Value:**
