The `add_ue_context` function adds a new UE context to the linked list by first checking if there is enough space in the allocated memory, and then creating a new `LTE_UE_CONTEXT_T` structure and adding it to the linked list. It also increments the size of the linked list by one.

The `free_ue_context_list` function frees the memory used by the linked list of UE contexts, and destroys the mutex that was created in the `initialize_ue_context_list` function."]

